course: dictionary
lesson: 2064
title: Consistency: the same, steady and smooth
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Consistency is a word with three meanings. The first is doing or behaving the same way every time, so people can rely on you. «Consistency means applying rules the same way to everyone.» A teacher who is consistent gives the same rule to every child, not a different rule for a friend.
explain: The second meaning is about texture: how thick, smooth or runny something is. Cooks talk about the consistency of a paste or a mixture, such as «a thick, smooth consistency». Here the word is about the feel of the mixture, not about behaviour.
explain: The third meaning is used in maths and logic. Consistency means that facts or rules do not contradict each other. «Consistency means treating similar cases in similar ways.» If two answers in a sum disagree, or a story says a door is locked and then someone walks through it with no key, something lacks consistency. Check the clues: words like same, steady, thick or contradict will tell you which meaning is in use.
fact: Consistency is a noun, and its plural is consistencies.
fact: «Consistency» means always acting, working or happening in the same way, steady and reliable.
fact: «Consistency» can also mean how thick, smooth or runny something is, like a paste or a mixture.
fact: In maths and logic, «consistency» means facts or rules do not contradict each other.
fact: Useful phrases: «the consistency of paste», «show consistency», «lack of consistency».
exercise: Mrs Patel gives the same homework rule to every child in the class. What quality is she showing? | *Consistency | Confusion | Curiosity | Speed
exercise: The cook says the sauce has the right consistency when it is smooth and runny. What does consistency describe here? | How old the sauce is | How many ingredients it has | How loud it is when it bubbles | *How thick or runny something is
exercise: A story says the door was locked, then a character walks straight through it with no key. What is the problem? | The author used a synonym | The door is too big | The character is hungry | *The story lacks consistency, because the facts contradict each other
test: The teacher punishes two pupils differently for the same mistake, with no real difference between them. What is missing? | *Consistency | Noise | Colour | Length
test: The recipe says «a thick, smooth consistency». What does consistency describe? | A school rule | *How thick or smooth the mixture is | A date on the calendar | The number of children in a team
exam: In a maths answer, what does it mean to show consistency? | The answer is wrong on purpose | The answer is very long | The answer is written in pretty handwriting | *Every step of the working agrees with the others, and no step contradicts another
